# The captain spaces us on the turn after the final verse, and the
# guard drags us back to the Hold -- where the keyboard is. Typing
# the word from the poetry chair gets "There's no keyboard in
# sight." and leaves the plotter (and the small receptacle inside
# it) sealed in the glass case forever.

wait

type "venchit"
get plotter

# The guard-stall turns are free: reclaim the towel from the drain
# and the gown from the hook (pocket fluff still inside it) before
# the airlock. The towel is the only one in the game, and the
# Bugblatter Beast of Traal will demand it; the fluff feeds the
# endgame plant.

get towel
get gown
wait

press green button

# Dark is authored sensory deprivation: for four turns the game
# insists you can sense nothing at all, and one of those denials
# ("You can't see anything...") happens to speak the refusal
# dialect, drawing one intentional warning on replay. On the fifth
# turn a sense returns -- hearing, for this seed -- which names the
# scenario (a star drive far above: the Heart of Gold).

listen
listen
listen
listen
listen

