# The guide's between-jumps ritual -- return to the Bridge and
# drop what you gained -- is not superstition: items carried into
# the whale's stomach (barring the unloseable thing, the fish, and
# no tea) are digested out of the timeline. The chipper is the
# tool Marvin will demand at the very end, so it waits here.

drop chipper
drop towel
press generator switch

# Tea-powered Dark works on a strict clock: the missing sense
# rotates hear -> smell -> see -> feel, one step per wait, and the
# matching sense verb connects without advancing the clock. (The
# words "put dangly bit in tea" also just started an interstellar
# war via freak wormhole -- the Careless Talk Costs Lives passage,
# which is required or the War Chamber can never be visited.)
# Occasional deprivation lines speak the refusal dialect and draw
# annotated warnings throughout the Dark visits.

